{
 "_about": "Synthetic encounter-summary evaluation corpus (docs/19 §8). No real patients. Each case drives the real API: typed intake through the fake provider (a keyword extractor, NOT an LLM), replayed OCR documents with explicit human review actions, and an optional triage run. `expect` holds the gold labels for the summary stage only. Small and hand-written: a regression and safety check, not evidence of clinical accuracy. Schema .4 adds image cases (the image model's output is REPLAYED from tests/fixtures/medgemma/model_outputs.json, or the built-in fake output; no image model runs) and interview cases (answers recorded through the interview API, English script only). Expected values were written from the intended behaviour before the cases were run.",
